# One kind of line ending in this repository: LF.
#
# It used to be mixed: 180 files out of 281 were stored with CRLF (72 .go,
# 50 .json, 43 .py), the rest with LF. The mixture is expensive. gofmt strips
# the CR and therefore called every Go file unformatted at once — a linter on
# such a repository checks nothing. And an edit script that guessed the endings
# of a particular file wrong rewrites the whole of it: a three-line diff turns
# into an eight-hundred-line one, and the real change is lost inside it.
#
# The working tree on Windows keeps whatever core.autocrlf gives it; git gets LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Run by bash under Windows: CRLF breaks the shebang.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
